From 2bb0f28232eba4965226f6ae6ce7f3d22c8396e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:44:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Tracked-secret scan over the index AND reachable history,
 with audit rail (from 832 T-410/T-938/T-939; AEF T-3572)

tools/tracked-secret-artifacts.py judges file NAMES (never content) for key material git is
publishing: DEFINITIVE names/extensions (.pem, id_rsa, .env, .fw-secret-key, ...) and ANNOUNCED
pairs (a secrecy word plus a credential noun at disjoint spans; a secret-store directory plus a
credential noun in the filename). --history covers every path in reachable history, which the
index cannot: it is how a purge reads complete while old commits still carry the blob.
Names of prose and source files (.md .py .sh .bats .js ...) are exempt from the two ANNOUNCED
rules: run on this tree, they flagged six files ABOUT the Watchtower secret key (task notes and
tests) and the rail would have FAILed on them. Keys hard-coded inside source are a content
question for the pre-commit scanner. Index hits FAIL; history-only hits WARN (rotate first; a
rewrite is Tier 0 and the operator's).
Teeth: tools/_t410-secret-artifact-teeth.sh, 14 legs incl. both directions of that exemption.
On this tree: index clean (19120 files), history clean (shallow clone, depth 50).
